    "body": "Problem: A previous change intended to skip the debounce if a change notification hadn't been sent in awhile (the first change after being idle) actually caused the change notifications to be sent every debounce interval while changes were actively happening. This effectively changed the debounce time into a rate limiting interval. The default of 150ms means that while changes are actively occurring in a buffer, a change notification was going out every 150ms.\r\n\r\nWith the recent consolidation of feature requests being tied to this change notification, that means that every active capability/feature was also firing every debounce interval instead of being debounced until changes settled.\r\n\r\nSolution: Turn the debounce back into an actual debounce. Even when coming back from idle, a change is likely to be followed by more changes, so didChange notifications (and the knock-on feature/capability requests) should actually debounce and wait for changes to stop before firing.\r\n\r\nThis reverts #16881.",
